{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "CONTROL · the automatic walker selection at stepper tempo 1 (the candidate of 2026-11-20, as measured) — promoted 2026-11-21 with tempo 2 as ...__ta30__t2",
    "description": "The stack of record with the after-touch record on (...__crh__hold__aft.json) and the walker selection holding the legs (PoseSequencer engage_follow 1): each walker's progress report (WalkerCompetence), the selector (WalkerSelect, trial_after_s 30: the stepper's first trial waits until the walker has 30 s of record), and the supply's outages per walker (WalkerOutage: a walker that browns out veto_n = 2 times inside a minute of its own driving loses the legs; the veto drops after the body has travelled 0.25 m under the other walker, doubled per repeat). The body models the brownout (OGMA_PICRAWLER_BROWNOUT 2 from this config's body_env: a reset is published on sense.hat_reset and every servo holds still for the 2.5 s outage). MEASURED (ledger 2026-11-20 evening, sim, 6 runs a cell, a signal): lockouts on obstacle grounds 3 of 24 runs against the walker alone 24 of 24; flat pace kept (arena 646 against 618 cm/min). Open: the vetoed walker keeps driving until the body stands (14 of 117 hand-overs waited over 3 s); flips at a hand-over from an extreme pose (8 in 72 runs). SCAFFOLDS: veto_n, relax_m, trial_after_s, the reset criterion (uncalibrated: rates order arms, they do not predict the robot's). LIVE: the [M] panel's HANDOVER row 'automatic selection' and its SUPPLY rows (brownout model 0/1/2, brownouts per minute to switch); [L] hands the legs over by hand while the selection is off. Body log: wr_* / sr_* (reports), ws_* (selector), wo_* (outages), bo_* (resets), ps_fol.",
